\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Never further than Thy Cross,
\par Never higher than Thy feet;
\par Here earth's precious things seem dross,
\par Here earth's bitter things grow sweet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Gazing thus our sins we see, 
\par Learn Thy love while gazing thus;
\par Sin which learn the Cross on thee,
\par Love which bore the Cross for us.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Here we learn to serve and give,
\par And, rejoicing, self deny;
\par Here we gather love to live,
\par Here we gather faith to die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Symbols of our liberty
\par And our serve here unite;
\par Captives, by Thy Cross set free,
\par Soldiers of Thy Cross, we fight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Pressing onward as we can,
\par Still to this our heart must tend;
\par Where our earliest hopes began;
\par There our last aspirings end.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Till amid the Hosts of light
\par We, in Thee redeemed, complete,
\par Through Thy Cross made pure band white,
\par Cast our Crowns before Thy feet.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

